**1. What I placed**

I added two text‑callouts on **sheet C‑101**.  
- The first callout points to the **left pavement edge** of the alignment; its text reads “Left Pavement Edge”.  
- The second callout points to the **right pavement edge**; its text reads “Right Pavement Edge”.  

Both callouts sit on the sheet space (paper inches), use the default annotative height (0.10 in), and the leader arrow is shown.

**2. Tool calls (in execution order)**  

```json
[
  {
    "name": "find_entities",
    "params": {
      "anchor": { "kind": "offset" },
      "visible_on": "C-101",
      "limit": 50
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "point_on_entity",
    "params": {
      "id": "BASE:LN-014",
      "sheet": "C-101",
      "where": "mid"
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "point_on_entity",
    "params": {
      "id": "BASE:LN-015",
      "sheet": "C-101",
      "where": "mid"
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "place_callout",
    "params": {
      "space": "C-101",
      "target_entity": "BASE:LN-014",
      "at": "mid",
      "position": [16.8, 9.6],        // 0.2 in left of the mid‑point
      "content": "Left Pavement Edge",
      "layer": "V-ANNO-TEXT",
      "height": 0.1,
      "arrow": true
    }
  },
  {
    "name": "place_callout",
    "params": {
      "space": "C-101",
      "target_entity": "BASE:LN-015",
      "at": "mid",
      "position": [17.3, 9.4],        // 0.2 in right of the mid‑point
      "content": "Right Pavement Edge",
      "layer": "V-ANNO-TEXT",
      "height": 0.1,
      "arrow": true
    }
  }
]
```

**3. Observations / Work‑arounds**

- The `find_entities` call returned two entities with IDs `BASE:LN-014` (offset –15 ft) and `BASE:LN-015` (offset +15 ft).  
- Since the callout positions must be specified in sheet inches, I asked the engine for the mid‑points of each entity in sheet space using `point_on_entity`; no manual conversion was needed.  
- No errors appeared during any command; the system automatically handled the placement of the leader arrow and the anchoring to the referenced alignment geometry.
